WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.700
Strip away the org charts and the software,
and every business runs on the same

2
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.550
thing: people with expertise, making
decisions and handing work to each other.

3
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.660
Now AI agents are joining that work.

4
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.500
The possibilities keep expanding.

5
00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.955
Better service.

6
00:00:27.025 --> 00:00:28.395
Faster responses.

7
00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:30.555
Work you couldn't take on before.

8
00:00:30.855 --> 00:00:33.745
But more capability isn't
the hard part anymore.

9
00:00:34.086 --> 00:00:36.625
Putting it to work across a business is.

10
00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:41.625
Reliable agents need a shared
picture of the business—what’s true,

11
00:00:41.665 --> 00:00:43.915
what’s promised, and who can change it.

12
00:00:44.251 --> 00:00:48.555
Watch how one missing commitment
turns a simple request into a problem.

13
00:00:49.105 --> 00:00:51.595
A customer asks for an earlier delivery.

14
00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:55.025
Operations finds capacity.

15
00:00:55.268 --> 00:00:57.425
Agents check staffing and cost.

16
00:00:57.612 --> 00:01:02.342
Then a conflict surfaces: that time
is already promised to someone else.

17
00:01:02.802 --> 00:01:04.492
Who can change the commitment?

18
00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:10.142
That decision needs someone with the
authority to make it—and the context to

19
00:01:10.182 --> 00:01:11.792
understand what it affects.

20
00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:13.925
Other work should keep moving.

21
00:01:14.225 --> 00:01:18.155
Getting this right is what lets
people and agents take on more.

22
00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:22.715
Getting it wrong turns speed in one
place into conflict in the next.

23
00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:26.625
At Volant Labs, we help businesses
build that way of working.

24
00:01:26.676 --> 00:01:31.326
We bring systems-engineering discipline to
the way people and agents work together.

25
00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:34.622
We work alongside your experts
to understand the work,

26
00:01:34.687 --> 00:01:39.297
clarify decision rights, and engineer
the context each decision depends on.

27
00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:43.255
Then we build and test the
capability in real work:

28
00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:46.538
what can proceed independently,
where judgment is needed,

29
00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:49.109
and how a change reaches
everyone it affects.

30
00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.419
Who decides?

31
00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:52.059
What does it depend on?

32
00:01:52.297 --> 00:01:53.419
What does it change?

33
00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:56.279
The same questions appear
in a design change,

34
00:01:56.319 --> 00:01:59.089
a financial plan,
or a customer commitment.

35
00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:01.679
The tools and boundaries will differ.

36
00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:04.159
The need to stay coordinated remains.

37
00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:11.161
As the work evolves, we help your
team keep the useful learning,

38
00:02:11.201 --> 00:02:15.039
correct outdated assumptions,
and get better at operating this way.

39
00:02:15.339 --> 00:02:18.869
Every decision made well
becomes context for the next.

40
00:02:19.619 --> 00:02:23.629
Our view is that this practice can
become a competitive advantage.

41
00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:27.979
A company learning to deliver better
work may start winning more of it.

42
00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:32.637
Access to the same models doesn't give
you the same operating experience.

43
00:02:33.287 --> 00:02:38.074
The next frontier is a living model of
your business—kept close to reality,

44
00:02:38.114 --> 00:02:40.915
and trusted by the people
and agents doing the work.

45
00:02:41.515 --> 00:02:43.605
That’s our focus at Volant Labs.

46
00:02:43.803 --> 00:02:48.485
Because scaling agents without trustworthy
context just scales the uncertainty.

47
00:02:48.855 --> 00:02:52.005
Let’s start with the work your
business can’t afford to get wrong.
